  "equipment_type": "Electric resistive steam humidifier",
  "applies_to": "Condair RS / RS II single and dual cylinder (A/B) resistive steam humidifiers.",
  "summary": "The Condair RS is an electric heating-element steam humidifier with one or two cylinders. The Integrated Controller exposes BACnet IP and MS/TP on-board. Objects report per-cylinder status, level, capacity, maintenance countdowns and safety chain inputs, plus two-channel setpoints and writable demand inputs for main and limiter signals.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 1001,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "BACnet is built into the Integrated Controller (RJ45 for BACnet IP, RS485 for MS/TP master or slave); it ships with the BACnet protocol set to Off.",
    "Factory Node ID (device instance) is 1001 and the MS/TP MAC is 127; BACnet IP uses UDP 47808 and supports registering with a BBMD.",
    "To command the unit over BACnet set Controls > Signal Settings > Source to BACnet; the demand/humidity AO must then be rewritten within the Signal Timeout (default 300 s) or the unit stops with warning W35.",
    "Points marked optional only report when that option is fitted; capacity, pressure and temperature units follow the controller's Metric/Imperial setting.",
    "Cylinder B objects only apply to dual-cylinder units; channel 2 is used for a limiter (e.g. supply-air high limit) when dual signal control is enabled.",
    "BI 28 is Furnace Fan on UL units and External Pipe Flush on CE units."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet on-board - Addendum manual for installation and operation (DL II, ME II, RS II, RO-E and Vita)",
    "doc_number": "2603582-F",
    "revision_date": "2026-07",
    "url": "https://www.condair.co.uk/consense/bms-communication-ic-2.0/am_bms_interface_bacnet_on_board_2603582_en.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Enable BACnet in the Integrated Controller, set the signal source to BACnet, and write demand or RH to AO 15012 (and a limiter value to AO 15014 if dual signal control is used) within the signal timeout. Read cylinder A/B status, the error status and code, and actual capacity.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AO 15012",
        "name": "RH or Demand CH1 via BACnet",
        "why": "Channel 1 demand or RH from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 15014",
        "name": "RH or Demand CH2 via BACnet",
        "why": "Channel 2 limiter signal (dual signal control)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 15102",
        "name": "Capacity Limitation",
        "why": "Capacity limitation"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 5109",
        "name": "Device Status Cyl. A",
        "why": "Cylinder A status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 5110",
        "name": "Device Status Cyl. B",
        "why": "Cylinder B status (dual units)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 5159",
        "name": "Error Status",
        "why": "Maintenance/error status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10020",
        "name": "ErrorWarning Code",
        "why": "Active error or warning code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10225",
        "name": "Actual Hum. Capacity",
        "why": "Actual humidifying capacity"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Set Menu > password 8808 > Controls > Signal Settings > Source to BACnet and pick the Control Mode (Demand, RH P or RH PI; On/Off also exists). With Source left at Analog the unit ignores BACnet control values.",
    "heartbeat": "When the signal source is not Analog, the demand/humidity value written over BACnet must be refreshed within the Signal Timeout (1-300 s, default 300 s). If it is not, warning W35 Signal Timeout is raised and the unit stops until a new value arrives, so the BMS must keep rewriting the AO.",
    "remote_sensors": "In Demand mode the BMS writes the required output (0-100 %) to the RH/Demand AO. In RH P or RH PI mode the BMS writes the measured humidity there and the controller's own setpoint, P-band and I-time AVs do the control. Do not connect a hard-wired demand or sensor signal while the BACnet signal is used. Channel 2 (AO 15014) is only active with dual signal control, typically a supply-air high limit.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet settings are under Menu > password 8808 > Network > BACnet Settings; the BACnet Protocol parameter ships Off (options MS/TP Master, MS/TP Slave, BACnet/IP) and the controller restarts after changing it.",
      "Node ID (device instance) defaults to 1001 (range 1-4194303); BACnet IP port defaults to 47808.",
      "IP addressing defaults to DHCP; if no DHCP server answers the controller falls back to an APIPA 169.254.x.x address.",
      "Foreign Device registration to a BBMD is Off by default; BBMD port 47808 and re-register time 10 are the factory values.",
      "MS/TP: MAC defaults to 127 (0-127 master, 0-254 slave), baud 9600 (up to 115200); fit jumper JP6 only on the first and last device, remove JP8, and tie GND between all devices."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Cylinder B objects only mean something on dual-cylinder units.",
      "BI 28 is Remote Furnace/Fan on UL units and External Pipe Flush on CE units.",
      "RS Drain AVs: write 1 to start, 0 to stop; a read of 100 means off.",
      "Capacity units follow the Metric/Imperial setting."
    ]
  },
